  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0516' consists of six tables: Customer, Pizza, Sales_Order, Income/Expenditure, Production_Plan, and Delivery_Content.\nThe Customer table is used to store customer information. It includes columns for Address, Customer_ID (which is the primary key), Name, and Phone.\nThe Pizza table is used to store pizza information. It includes columns for Flavor, Ingredients, Pizza_ID (which is the primary key), and Stock.\nThe Sales_Order table is used to store sales order information. It includes columns for Customer_ID (which is not null and references the Customer table), Expected_Delivery_Date, Order_ID (which is the primary key), and Status.\nThe Income/Expenditure table is used to store income and expenditure records. It includes columns for Amount, Description, Pizza_ID (which is not null and references the Pizza table), Record_ID (which is the primary key), Time, and Type.\nThe Production_Plan table is used to store production plan information. It includes columns for Order_ID (which is not null and references the Sales_Order table) and Pizza_ID (which is not null and references the Pizza table), Production_Quantity, and Production_Sequence. The primary key of this table is a combination of Order_ID and Pizza_ID.\nFinally, the Delivery_Content table is used to store delivery content information. It includes columns for Delivery_Time, Order_ID (which is not null and references the Sales_Order table), Record_ID (which is the primary key), and Status.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements:\n1.Customer: Each customer needs to record basic information, including Customer ID, Name, Phone, and Address.\n2.Sales Order: Each customer can have multiple sales orders. Each sales order contains Order ID, Customer ID, Pizza ID, Quantity, Expected Delivery Date, and Order Status.\n3.Pizza: Each type of pizza needs to record Pizza ID, Flavor, Ingredients, and Stock. Pizza ID is the Primary key used to uniquely identify each pizza.\n4.Production Plan: A production plan is generated based on sales orders. Each production plan records Order ID, Pizza ID, Production Sequence, and Production Quantity.\n5.Income/Expenditure: Records each income or expenditure. The record includes Record ID, Type (Income or Expenditure), Amount, Time, Description, and the related Pizza ID. Each income/expenditure record can be associated with multiple pizzas, for tracking and analyzing financial data related to pizzas.\n6.Delivery Content: Records the delivery information for each order, including Record ID, Order ID, Delivery Time, and Delivery Status. Each delivery record is associated with a sales order and records the delivery details.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0516.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0516\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pizza` (\n  `pizza_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `flavor` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `ingredients` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stock` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`pizza_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `expected_delivery_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `income_expenditure` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `pizza_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `income_expenditure_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`pizza_id`) REFERENCES `pizza` (`pizza_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `production_plan` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `pizza_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `production_quantity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `production_sequence` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`, `pizza_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `production_plan_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `sales_order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `production_plan_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`pizza_id`) REFERENCES `pizza` (`pizza_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `delivery_content` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `delivery_content_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `sales_order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
